  "registration": "Depth increment 2, attempt A420. Split decided 2026-11-12 before any result: development assets A-C, held out D-E. Method, scorer and pass margin frozen before the one held-out run. What it shows: the tool derive option applies a user-declared vocabulary faithfully and groups by it, and a 10-rule vocabulary written from A-C (including their publisher codes) carries over to D-E under one publisher coding scheme. The vocabulary is a per-dataset profile artifact, not part of the product. It does not show what a user without a key would write (see the post-hoc key-free control run) and does not measure engineering correctness: the key was made by keyword rules over the same text. Originals are not redistributed: the suite opts in to optional_cache, so in a clean clone it is UNVERIFIED and its committed report stands as recorded.",
